Source: libmali-cix
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), meson, pkgconf
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/ginkage/libmali-cix

Package: libmali-cix
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libegl1, libglvnd0, libvulkan1, ocl-icd-libopencl1
Recommends: cix-gpu-dkms
Conflicts: cix-gpu-umd
Replaces: cix-gpu-umd
Description: Arm Mali vendor userspace driver for the CIX P1 (Mali-G720)
 libmali r54p1 (GLES, EGL, Vulkan, OpenCL, GBM) for the CIX P1 / CD8180 GPU,
 next to Mesa: libEGL_mali, a glvnd EGL vendor that routes each application
 to libmali or to Mesa (zink on libmali's Vulkan) per /etc/mali/app.json; a
 libgbm.so.1 wrapper; the Vulkan window system integration layer; the CSF
 firmware; manifests, a dma-heap udev rule, and mali-switch.
 .
 Everything is installed inert under <libdir>/mali. "mali-switch mali" puts it
 on the linker path and blacklists panthor (needs cix-gpu-dkms); "mali-switch
 panthor" goes back to panthor and Mesa. Both take effect after a reboot.
